 {"id": "PEDS-U226", "ch": 27, "n": 5, "title": "Management of Asthma — Overview & Stepwise Therapy (Age 6–11 yr)", "sec": "Management of asthma · p121", "qs": ["PEDS-C27-051", "PEDS-C27-052", "PEDS-C27-053", "PEDS-C27-054", "PEDS-C27-055", "PEDS-C27-056", "PEDS-C27-057", "PEDS-C27-058", "PEDS-C27-059", "PEDS-C27-060", "PEDS-C27-061", "PEDS-C27-062", "PEDS-C27-063", "PEDS-C27-064", "PEDS-C27-065", "PEDS-C27-066", "PEDS-C27-067", "PEDS-C27-068", "PEDS-C27-069"], "guide": "Based on Global Initiative Network for Asthma (GINA) guidelines. Management → identification & elimination of exacerbating factors + pharmacotherapy (long-term management, acute exacerbations). Age > 12 yr: managed as in adults. Age 6 to 11 yr: stepwise management. Step 1 reliever therapy → short-acting β-agonist (SABA) (SOS for sudden exacerbation of symptoms). Steps — I: < 2/month → whenever SABA taken → ICS low dose; II: > 2/month, not daily → daily low dose ICS; III: daily symptoms + night symptoms ≥ 1/week → daily low dose ICS + LABA OR daily medium dose ICS; IV: daily + night symptoms ≥ 1/week + low lung function → daily medium dose ICS + LABA OR high dose ICS; V: uncontrolled on step IV → daily high dose ICS + LABA (+/−), biological agents (last resort)."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U227", "ch": 27, "n": 6, "title": "Asthma Drugs — SABA, LABA, ICS Doses & Biological Agents", "sec": "Pharmacotherapy · p121", "qs": ["PEDS-C27-070", "PEDS-C27-071", "PEDS-C27-072", "PEDS-C27-073", "PEDS-C27-074", "PEDS-C27-075", "PEDS-C27-076", "PEDS-C27-077", "PEDS-C27-078", "PEDS-C27-079", "PEDS-C27-080", "PEDS-C27-081", "PEDS-C27-082", "PEDS-C27-083", "PEDS-C27-084", "PEDS-C27-085"], "guide": "SABA: short-acting β-agonist. LABA: long-acting β-agonist (formoterol) — synergistic effect with steroid; steroid sparing effect (long-term). ICS: inhaled corticosteroid — budesonide used. Low dose: 200 to 400 mcg; medium dose: 400 to 800 mcg; high dose: > 800 mcg. Biological agents: immunomodulatory monoclonal antibodies — omalizumab (anti-IgE), mepolizumab (anti-IL5), dupilumab (anti-IL4 receptor), anti-TSLP (thymic stromal lymphopoietin): new drug."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U228", "ch": 27, "n": 7, "title": "Asthma in Age < 5 yr (Preschool)", "sec": "Age < 5 yr (preschool) · p122", "qs": ["PEDS-C27-086", "PEDS-C27-087", "PEDS-C27-088", "PEDS-C27-089", "PEDS-C27-090", "PEDS-C27-091", "PEDS-C27-092", "PEDS-C27-093", "PEDS-C27-094", "PEDS-C27-095", "PEDS-C27-096", "PEDS-C27-097", "PEDS-C27-098", "PEDS-C27-099"], "guide": "Age < 5 yr (preschool): asthma may resolve > 5 yr in some patients. Classification of patient: episodic wheeze (during viral infection), multitrigger wheeze (during respiratory infection + other triggers: cold, exertion, food). Asthma probability: ↑ probability for future asthma (requires treatment) if symptoms last > 10 d after URI AND > 3 episodes. Treatment: controller — daily low-dose ICS therapy + reliever therapy — SABA → review after 2 months → improvement → stop treatment; no improvement → treat as per age 6 to 11 guidelines."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U229", "ch": 27, "n": 8, "title": "Acute Exacerbation — Classification of Episodes", "sec": "Acute exacerbation — classification · p122", "qs": ["PEDS-C27-100", "PEDS-C27-101", "PEDS-C27-102", "PEDS-C27-103", "PEDS-C27-104", "PEDS-C27-105", "PEDS-C27-106", "PEDS-C27-107", "PEDS-C27-108", "PEDS-C27-109", "PEDS-C27-110", "PEDS-C27-111", "PEDS-C27-112", "PEDS-C27-113", "PEDS-C27-114"], "guide": "Classification of exacerbation episodes — Sensorium: mild normal, moderate anxious, severe agitated. Dyspneal retractions: mild absent, moderate moderately present, severe severe. SpO2: mild > 95%, moderate 90–95%, severe < 90%. PEFR (% of predicted): mild > 80%, moderate 60–80%, severe < 60%. PEFR: peak expiratory flow rate."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U230", "ch": 27, "n": 9, "title": "Acute Exacerbation — Management by Severity", "sec": "Acute exacerbation — management · p122", "qs": ["PEDS-C27-115", "PEDS-C27-116", "PEDS-C27-117", "PEDS-C27-118", "PEDS-C27-119", "PEDS-C27-120", "PEDS-C27-121", "PEDS-C27-122", "PEDS-C27-123", "PEDS-C27-124", "PEDS-C27-125", "PEDS-C27-126", "PEDS-C27-127", "PEDS-C27-128"], "guide": "Mild: salbutamol in metered dose inhalers (MDI) — 4–10 puff every 20 minutes. Moderate: salbutamol + ipratropium (centrally acting anti-cholinergics) + O2 to keep SpO2 > 95% + oral prednisolone. Severe: nebulised salbutamol + ipratropium + oral prednisolone or iv hydrocortisone + inj magnesium sulphate."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U231", "ch": 27, "n": 10, "title": "Asthma Medication Devices", "sec": "Asthma medication devices · p123", "qs": ["PEDS-C27-129", "PEDS-C27-130", "PEDS-C27-131", "PEDS-C27-132", "PEDS-C27-133", "PEDS-C27-134", "PEDS-C27-135", "PEDS-C27-136", "PEDS-C27-137", "PEDS-C27-138", "PEDS-C27-139", "PEDS-C27-140", "PEDS-C27-141"], "guide": "Based on age of child: ≥ 12 yr — MDI; 4 to 12 yr — MDI + spacer (allows drug to be suspended in air → inhaled over few breaths); < 4 yr — MDI + spacer + face mask. Rotahaler (not commonly used) — mouth piece for inhalation of powdered rotacap; hole for inserting rotacap; tin; rota chamber: rota cap powdered on twisting."},
